window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-6e7a4d8561190362"]={"key":"ny_b1-6e7a4d8561190362","group":"ny_b1","uid":"6e7a4d8561190362","rank":57,"title":"ironvale hydraulic filter claim findings memo","occupation":"buyers_purchasing_agents","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You’re Joaquin Cordova, the senior buyer at Ironvale Media, and Mirela Havlicek needs your revised findings before tomorrow’s cross-functional claim-allocation meeting. A hydraulic filter head supplied through Peatmoor Trust failed at our customer, which has presented a £310,000 line-down claim. The current draft attributes the failure to transit mishandling, but that conclusion was written before the latest review comments and logger information arrived. The receiving photographs, both versions of the advance shipping notice, the forwarder’s temperature record, the relevant purchasing terms, the technical note, Peatmoor Trust’s position and the marked-up draft are all consolidated in `claim_evidence_bundle.pdf`. The evidence looks close to a tidy transit story, but it is not tidy: the temperature record has a nine-hour gap that could represent missing measurements rather than an adverse condition, while the ASN discrepancy could reflect repacking rather than a change to the part. Some records share a shipment reference but do not establish a causal connection. Peatmoor Trust continues to maintain that the unit left it conforming.\n\nReplace the draft with a final findings memorandum named `hydraulic_filter_claim_findings.docx`, written into the top level of your working directory using exactly that filename. Keep the complete document to four pages or fewer, including the revision note. It is for Mirela, Quality, Logistics, Finance and Legal, so make it readable by stakeholders who have not worked through the evidence bundle themselves. Treat England and Wales as the relevant jurisdiction and state the position as at 30 September 2025. This is a procurement findings document, not external correspondence or a legal opinion.\n\nThe revised memorandum must do the following: (1) give one clear, evidence-bounded finding on where the failure most likely originated and state the confidence that the available record justifies; (2) distinguish the likely physical origin from contractual claim allocation, rather than treating delivery risk, causation and recoverability as the same question; (3) address the competing explanations raised by the photographs, the two ASNs, the temperature-log gap and Peatmoor Trust’s statement, including material fragments that cannot presently be connected; (4) tie important factual statements to identifiers, timestamps, image references or document references that Peatmoor Trust’s insurer can locate in the bundle; (5) state what the £310,000 represents without presenting it as agreed, validated or recoverable unless the evidence supports that status; (6) give a concrete disposition for the allocation meeting and identify any checks that must occur before the position can become final, with owners and timing suitable for execution; and (7) include a compact revision note identifying what changed from the marked-up draft and why.\n\nDo not invent test results, temperatures, contractual wording, monetary breakdowns or missing chain-of-custody events. Where the record cannot support a conclusion or a required check cannot be completed, the memorandum must provide a usable path for recording and escalating that limitation rather than assuming the evidence will become available. Technical defect confirmation belongs to Quality, interpretation of enforceability and insurance coverage belongs to Legal or the relevant insurer, and claim validation involves Finance; the memorandum should still make the procurement finding Mirela requested without taking over those functions. End with the decision to be carried into the meeting, not with a generic list of possible next steps.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/claim_evidence_bundle.pdf` — Consolidated evidence bundle containing the marked-up draft, review comments, receiving photographs, both ASNs, forwarder temperature records, purchasing terms, technical note, claim notice and Peatmoor Trust statement.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `hydraulic_filter_claim_findings.docx` — Revised cross-functional findings memorandum supporting the claim-allocation decision. (Write the file at the top level of the working directory using the exact filename hydraulic_filter_claim_findings.docx.; The complete document, including its revision note, must not exceed four rendered pages.; Use England and Wales as the jurisdiction and state the position as at 30 September 2025.; Provide one evidence-bounded finding on the most likely origin and a concrete disposition for the allocation meeting.; Do not invent figures, test results, temperatures, contractual language or chain-of-custody events.; End with the decision to be carried into the allocation meeting.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/claim_evidence_bundle.pdf","bytes":11951,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/a28c63d0284eb6ddf051da1e13e3d9b773f20dbd0bfabf749c3c51c626529515.pdf","sha256":"a28c63d0284eb6ddf051da1e13e3d9b773f20dbd0bfabf749c3c51c626529515","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"                                            CLAIM EVIDENCE BUNDLE\n Hydraulic filter head — customer line-down claim | compiled 30 September 2025\n\n\n Control note. This internal compilation preserves the source labels used below. It includes the prior marked-up draft and review\n comments, not a finding of fact. Records relate to PO IV-44718 unless stated otherwise.\n\nComponent                              Hydraulic filter head | Part HFX-6200-17 | Serial HFH-25-0917\nShipment                               PMT-UK-240925-08 | Forwarder consignment FWD-7749031\nCustomer notice                        CN-047, dated 29 Sep 2025 — £310,000 line-down cost claimed\nBundle index                           DRAFT-01; REV-01; ASN-01/02; RCV-01/02; LOG-01; TERMS-01; TECH-01; PT-01; CN-047\n\n\n Evidence map\n\n The items are placed in date/source order where practical. Image references RCV-01 and RCV-02 are receiving photographs\n reconstructed from the receiving record, with original captions and timestamps retained.\n\n\n\n\nIronvale Media | Claim evidence bundle | Internal compilation                                                                Page 1\n\f   DRAFT-01 — marked-up failure-origin memorandum (superseded)\n Draft conclusion: “The temperature excursion during carriage caused the hydraulic filter-head failure. Allocate the customer’s\n £310,000 claim to the forwarder.”\n\n Margin mark: Delete / unsupported. The log has a gap; it does not record an excursion. Do not equate delivery risk with cause\n or recovery.\n\n\n REV-01 — review comments (M. Havlicek / Quality / Legal)\n\nREV-01.1                               Replace the assertion of a recorded temperature excursion; identify the missing-data interval and\n                                       the logger diagnostic.\nREV-01.2                               Address revised ASN and Peatmoor’s repacking notation. Explain what that record does and does\n                                       not prove.\nREV-01.3                               Separate likely physical origin, delivery/risk provision, contractual liability, insurer coverage and\n                                       validation of the customer amount.\nREV-01.4                               Give insurer-locatable citations and make non-connections visible; name owners and a route if\n                                       evidence cannot be obtained.\nREV-01.5                               End on the proposed allocation-meeting position.\n\n\n\n\nIronvale Media | Claim evidence bundle | Internal compilation                                                                             Page 2\n\f                         ASN-01 — Advance Shipping Notice (original)\n Peatmoor Trust | issued 24 Sep 2025, 09:14\n\nDocument number                        ASN-PT-240925-118\nPurchase order                         IV-44718\nShipment / carrier                     PMT-UK-240925-08 / FWD-7749031\nLine                                   1 — Hydraulic filter head, HFX-6200-17; serial HFH-25-0917\nPackage                                1 carton — OEM-sealed carton; 47 × 33 × 28 cm; gross weight 18.4 kg\nStatus                                 Ready for collection\n\n\n\n                         ASN-02 — Advance Shipping Notice (revised)\n Peatmoor Trust | issued 24 Sep 2025, 12:36\n\nDocument number                        ASN-PT-240925-118-R1\nPurchase order                         IV-44718\nShipment / carrier                     PMT-UK-240925-08 / FWD-7749031\nLine                                   1 — Hydraulic filter head, HFX-6200-17; serial HFH-25-0917\nPackage                                1 carton — repacked by Peatmoor after outer label damage; replacement transit carton; 49 × 35\n                                       × 30 cm; gross weight 19.1 kg\nStatus                                 Ready for collection\n\n\n CARR-01 — forwarder collection scan: FWD-7749031; Peatmoor Trust despatch point; 24 Sep 2025, 15:10. No event narrative\n is recorded in this scan.\n\n\n\n\nIronvale Media | Claim evidence bundle | Internal compilation                                                                 Page 3\n\f             RCV-01 / RCV-02 — receiving photographs and captions\n Ironvale receiving record, shipment PMT-UK-240925-08 / serial HFH-25-0917\n\n\n          RCV-01 — 25 Sep 2025, 10:42                               RCV-02 — 25 Sep 2025, 10:44\n          Exterior carton at receipt. Carton faces shown intact;    Internal packing / port. Port protector detached; port\n          no obvious crushing, puncture or wetting visible.         exposed with visible debris. No conclusion in the\n                                                                    record on when this condition arose.\n\n\n\n\n Receiving note RN-928: “Carton externally clean / no visible transit damage. Internal port cap loose.” The note identifies the\n shipment and serial above; it does not record an opening, impact, or custody event before receipt.\n\n\n\n\nIronvale Media | Claim evidence bundle | Internal compilation                                                                     Page 4\n\f                      LOG-01 — forwarder temperature record extract\n Consignment FWD-7749031 | logger TL-44-218 | storage requirement: 5°C to 35°C (SPEC-01)\n\n24 Sep 2025, 15:20                     18.2°C — recorded; within storage requirement\n24 Sep 2025, 15:20 to 25 Sep           No readings — 8 h 58 min missing interval\n2025, 00:18\n25 Sep 2025, 00:16                     Diagnostic: LOW POWER / RESTART FLAG\n25 Sep 2025, 00:18                     17.9°C — recorded; within storage requirement\nLog note                               The diagnostic makes sensor/power interruption plausible. It does not identify the reason for the\n                                       missing readings. No record in LOG-01 records an excursion, opening, drop, impact or other\n                                       handling event.\n\n\n SPEC-01 — product handling extract: “Store and transport at 5°C to 35°C.” No temperature is stated for the missing interval.\n\n\n\n\nIronvale Media | Claim evidence bundle | Internal compilation                                                                        Page 5\n\f          TERMS-01 — purchasing terms extract (PO IV-44718, rev. 6)\nClause 1.3                             Governing law: England and Wales.\nClause 7.2                             Delivery: DAP Ironvale Distribution Centre, Coventry (Incoterms® 2020). Risk passes on physical\n                                       delivery at the named place.\nClause 12.1                            Supplier liability is subject to the agreement’s exclusions, limitations and applicable cap.\nClause 12.3                            Neither party is liable for indirect or consequential loss, subject to the agreement and applicable\n                                       law.\n\n\n\n The extract is supplied for commercial review. It contains no determination of cause, enforceability, coverage or amount.\n\n\n\n\nIronvale Media | Claim evidence bundle | Internal compilation                                                                          Page 6\n\f                         TECH-01 — preliminary Quality technical note\n QTN-25-144 | 28 Sep 2025 | preliminary\n\n Observed failure is compatible with contamination or ingress at the exposed port. This preliminary note cannot determine when\n or where material entered, whether the protector detached before or after handoff, or identify a responsible actor. Further\n technical examination is required for defect confirmation.\n\n\n                              PT-01 — Peatmoor Trust written position\n 28 Sep 2025\n\n “Peatmoor Trust maintains that the unit left our facility conforming. Incoming inspection/conformity record IR-910 supports this\n position.” IR-910 is dated 23 Sep 2025, 08:45. PT-01 provides no post-repack test, seal record or condition photograph; ASN-02\n records repacking on 24 Sep 2025.\n\n\n                                       CN-047 — customer claim notice\n 29 Sep 2025\n\n Customer presents a £310,000 line-down cost claim following reported failure. The notice supplies no completed validation,\n agreed breakdown, admission, mitigation review or recoverability determination.\n\n\n\n\nIronvale Media | Claim evidence bundle | Internal compilation                                                                 Page 7\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/hydraulic_filter_claim_findings.docx","bytes":40582,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/3df3f1d3f94d608d5c30779a88d09281e068524800ba412d24f390d37f3732f7.docx","sha256":"3df3f1d3f94d608d5c30779a88d09281e068524800ba412d24f390d37f3732f7","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"IRONVALE MEDIA — INTERNAL PROCUREMENT FINDINGS MEMORANDUM\nHydraulic filter head claim | Position as at 30 September 2025 | England and Wales\nTo\nFrom\nSubject\nMirela Havlicek; Quality; Logistics; Finance; Legal\nJoaquin Cordova, Senior Buyer\nPO IV-44718 — HFX-6200-17 / serial HFH-25-0917; customer line-down claim\nProcurement finding and meeting disposition\nFinding. On the available record, the most likely condition-compromise window is Peatmoor Trust’s documented repacking or associated pre-handover handling, not established transit temperature exposure. Confidence is moderate: ASN-02 documents an intervention before CARR-01 handoff, while the receipt photographs and log weaken the simple transit account. This is a provisional procurement finding, not proof of a particular damaging act, actor, or mechanism.\nDecision requested. The customer has presented a £310,000 line-down claim (CN-047). It is neither admitted nor validated, and this memorandum does not allocate it finally. Carry the provisional Peatmoor repack/pre-handover origin finding into tomorrow’s allocation meeting; withdraw the draft’s assertion of proven transit-temperature damage; do not admit or finally allocate £310,000 pending the specified checks.\nTraceable record and comparative assessment\nSequence / source\nWhat the record supports — and does not support\n23 Sep, 08:45 — IR-910 (quoted PT-01)\nPeatmoor’s incoming inspection/conformity material predates the next-day repack. It supports Peatmoor’s stated position only; it does not establish post-repack condition at handoff.\n24 Sep, 09:14 — ASN-01 / ASN-PT-240925-118; 12:36 — ASN-02 / ASN-PT-240925-118-R1\nBoth identify PO IV-44718, part HFX-6200-17, serial HFH-25-0917 and shipment PMT-UK-240925-08. ASN-01 says OEM-sealed carton, 47×33×28 cm, 18.4 kg. ASN-02 says “repacked by Peatmoor after outer label damage,” replacement transit carton, 49×35×30 cm, 19.1 kg. This documents a handling opportunity, not damage or a changed part.\n24 Sep, 15:10 — CARR-01\nForwarder collection scan for FWD-7749031 at Peatmoor. The scan contains no event narrative.\n24 Sep 15:20 to 25 Sep 00:18 — LOG-01\nA 8 h 58 min absence of readings, not a recorded excursion. 18.2°C before and 17.9°C after are within SPEC-01’s 5°C to 35°C range. LOW POWER / RESTART at 00:16 makes sensor/power interruption plausible, not proven; no temperature, opening, drop or carrier event is recorded for the gap.\n25 Sep, 10:42–10:44 — RCV-01/02; RN-928\nRCV-01 shows intact exterior carton with no obvious crushing, puncture or wetting. RCV-02/RN-928 show detached/loose port protector, exposed port and visible debris. This weakens an obvious external-impact transit theory but cannot time the internal condition or identify who caused it.\n28–29 Sep — TECH-01; PT-01; CN-047\nTECH-01 says the failure is compatible with contamination/ingress but cannot locate its introduction or identify an actor. PT-01’s “left conforming” assertion is party evidence, unaccompanied by a post-repack test, seal record or condition photo. CN-047 presents the £310,000 line-down claim without validated quantum or mitigation.\nAssessment. Relative support. Repack/pre-handover handling is best supported as the origin window because a documented intervention precedes handoff and post-repack condition is unverified. Transit mishandling remains possible but is weaker on this record: there is no measured temperature breach or recorded carrier event, and externally intact packaging is inconsistent with a simple external-impact account. A manufacturing defect is not established: the preliminary technical note is compatible with ingress and cannot trace timing or origin.\nLimits. The principal non-connections remain material: no measured temperature breach; no direct evidence links the logger gap to damage; and no direct evidence links the repack to protector detachment or contamination. Those limits are why the finding remains moderate-confidence and provisional.\nCommercial boundaries — England and Wales\nTerms. TERMS-01 clause 1.3 selects England and Wales. Clause 7.2 states DAP Ironvale Distribution Centre, Coventry (Incoterms® 2020), with risk passing on physical delivery at the named place. That delivery/risk provision may matter to commercial allocation; it does not prove when the condition arose or who legally caused it. Factual origin, contractual risk transfer, legal liability, and insurer coverage are separate questions.\nClaim position. Under TERMS-01 clauses 12.1 and 12.3, any downstream line-down recovery requires Legal review of contractual scope, causation, remoteness/foreseeability, mitigation, exclusions and any applicable cap; coverage is for the relevant insurer. Finance must validate CN-047’s quantum and mitigation evidence. Neither the £310,000 amount nor any liability is admitted by this procurement position.\nChecks required before final allocation\nOwner / deadline\nSpecific check and disposition if unavailable\nProcurement — issue 30 Sep; response by 2 Oct (2 business days)\nRequest Peatmoor’s post-repack condition photos, packing checklist, seal/closure record, repack operator record and any post-repack test. If unavailable, record the request/response in the claim file, retain the pre-handover limitation, and escalate residual supplier-allocation choice to Legal and Mirela.\nLogistics / claims — request 30 Sep; response by 2 Oct\nRequest forwarder’s raw logger diagnostic/export, device power/restart history and custody/event records for FWD-7749031. If unavailable, record the gap as unresolved—not an excursion—and take no carrier allocation inference; escalate carrier-reservation decision to Legal/claims lead.\nQuality — report by 3 Oct\nConfirm whether inspection can establish a technical defect, contamination/ingress indicators, or any reliable timing limitation. If examination cannot be completed, log the reason and retain TECH-01’s limitation.\nFinance and Legal — 3 Oct review\nFinance obtains CN-047 substantiation and mitigation records; Legal reviews TERMS-01, enforceability, recoverability and insurer/claim-notice posture. If evidence is unavailable, Finance records quantum unvalidated and Legal/Mirela decide documented reserve/escalation; no amount is inferred.\nRevision note\nREV-02. Replaces DRAFT-01’s unsupported conclusion that a temperature excursion in carriage caused the failure and its forwarder-allocation recommendation. Incorporates LOG-01’s 8 h 58 min missing-data interval and restart diagnostic; adds ASN-02 repack evidence, photo/technical limitations, traceable citations, ownership and an unavailable-record escalation path; and separates provisional physical origin from risk, liability, coverage and quantum.\nDECISION TO CARRY INTO THE ALLOCATION MEETING: retain the moderate-confidence, provisional Peatmoor repack/pre-handover origin finding; withdraw proven-transit-temperature causation; and do not finally allocate or admit the customer’s £310,000 line-down claim unless and until the named checks are recorded and reviewed.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required DOCX is present, opens successfully and is not corrupt.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted file hydraulic_filter_claim_findings.docx.","grader_hint":"Open the DOCX with a standard Office-compatible parser or application and confirm that it contains readable document content."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The complete memorandum, including the revision note, renders to no more than four pages.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered hydraulic_filter_claim_findings.docx.","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX using a standard office renderer and count all pages; the maximum is four."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum identifies England and Wales as the relevant jurisdiction and states the position as at 30 September 2025.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Jurisdiction and date language in the memorandum.","grader_hint":"Accept normal variants such as 'laws of England and Wales' and 'as at 30 September 2025' if both jurisdiction and date are explicit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum gives one unambiguous finding that the most likely condition-compromise window was Peatmoor Trust’s documented repacking or associated pre-handover handling, rather than asserting that transit temperature exposure was the established origin.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Executive finding, analysis and concluding decision.","grader_hint":"The wording may vary, but it must select the Peatmoor repack/pre-handover handling window as most likely. A memo that presents Peatmoor and transit as equally likely does not satisfy this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The finding is calibrated as a most-likely or provisional factual assessment and does not claim that a specific damaging act, actor or mechanism has been proved.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Finding and confidence language.","grader_hint":"Look for language such as 'most likely,' 'moderate confidence' or an equivalent limitation, paired with an express recognition that the precise act or mechanism is not established."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The origin finding, confidence level and recommended meeting disposition agree everywhere they appear in the document.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary, body analysis, revision note and final decision.","grader_hint":"Compare all statements of conclusion. There must be no section reverting to a confirmed transit-causation finding or a materially different allocation position."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum reconstructs the relevant sequence from Peatmoor documentation and repacking through carrier handoff, receipt and later reported failure without inserting unsupported custody events.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Chronology or narrative analysis.","grader_hint":"Check the sequence against the bundle. Exact formatting is immaterial, but order and event attribution must be accurate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum correctly links the two ASNs using the shared purchase order, part, serial or shipment identifiers shown in the bundle.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"ASN discussion and cited identifiers.","grader_hint":"Confirm that the identifiers cited are actually common to both ASNs and are transcribed accurately."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum accurately describes the material differences between the original and revised ASN, including the revised record’s repacking notation and changed shipment particulars.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"ASN comparison in the memorandum.","grader_hint":"Compare the description to both ASNs. It should capture the repacking notation and relevant changed particulars without turning the discrepancy itself into proof of damage."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The ASN discrepancy is treated as evidence of an intervention or handling opportunity, not as proof that the component was defective or damaged during repacking.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Interpretation of the ASN evidence.","grader_hint":"Credit only if the memo expressly or clearly distinguishes the documented repack from an unproved damaging act."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The receiving-photo account accurately reports the intact exterior packaging condition and the detached port protector or exposed-port condition visible in the referenced photographs.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Photo findings with image references.","grader_hint":"Compare the memo’s description with the receiving photographs and captions in the bundle."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum recognizes that intact exterior packaging weakens a simple external-impact transit theory but does not establish when or by whom the internal condition arose.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Photo analysis.","grader_hint":"The document must use the photographs in both directions: as evidence against obvious external impact and as insufficient to time the internal condition."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The temperature-log discussion gives the gap’s duration and relevant time bounds consistently with the raw log.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Temperature-log analysis.","grader_hint":"Compare the cited duration and endpoints to the bundle. Allow ordinary rounding of the approximately nine-hour interval, but not a materially different gap."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum correctly treats the logger gap as an absence of readings rather than a recorded temperature excursion.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Temperature-log finding.","grader_hint":"Credit only if the memo clearly states that the gap does not itself show an out-of-range temperature."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum notes that recorded values before and after the gap remain within the applicable storage range and does not invent values for the missing interval.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Temperature evidence compared with the product or purchasing requirement in the bundle.","grader_hint":"Verify any stated values or ranges against the bundle and confirm that no interpolated or assumed temperature is presented as observed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The logger diagnostic or restart evidence is identified as a plausible sensor or power explanation without being promoted to a proven explanation for the gap.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Logger reliability analysis.","grader_hint":"Look for balanced treatment: the diagnostic supports a non-temperature explanation but does not conclusively establish one."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum does not claim that the carrier opened, dropped, overheated or otherwise mishandled the shipment during the unrecorded interval.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All transit and logger statements.","grader_hint":"Review the whole memo for affirmative carrier-event claims. Conditional statements identifying such events as unverified are acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Peatmoor Trust’s assertion that the part left conforming is characterized as a party statement rather than independent proof.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Discussion of Peatmoor Trust’s statement.","grader_hint":"Credit if the source and evidential status of the assertion are clear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum recognizes that Peatmoor Trust’s cited inspection or conformity material predates the documented repack and does not establish post-repack condition at handoff.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparison of the Peatmoor statement, inspection record and revised ASN.","grader_hint":"Check dates and scope in the bundle. The key distinction is pre-repack evidence versus condition after repacking."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The technical note is used only for the limited proposition it supports, such as compatibility with contamination or ingress, and is not represented as identifying when or where the condition was introduced.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Technical-causation discussion.","grader_hint":"Compare the memo with the technical note’s qualifications. It must not convert a compatible mechanism into a traced origin."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum explicitly identifies the principal non-connections: no measured temperature breach, no direct evidence linking the log gap to damage, and no direct evidence linking the documented repack to detachment of the protector or introduction of contamination.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Limitations or evidentiary-gap discussion.","grader_hint":"Equivalent wording is acceptable, but all three logical gaps must be conveyed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Manufacturing defect, repack/handling compromise and transit mishandling are treated as competing origin hypotheses, with their relative support assessed rather than merely listed.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparative findings analysis.","grader_hint":"Credit if the memo explains why repack/pre-handover handling is best supported, transit is unresolved but weaker, and manufacturing origin is not established by the current record."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum distinguishes factual cause or origin, contractual risk transfer, legal liability and insurance coverage as separate questions.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Commercial and doctrinal analysis.","grader_hint":"All four concepts need not be in one sentence, but the memo must not collapse them into a single conclusion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The delivery term or risk-transfer provision is described accurately while making clear that risk transfer does not by itself prove when a defect arose or who legally caused it.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Purchasing-terms discussion.","grader_hint":"Compare the stated delivery term with the bundle and look for the required doctrinal limitation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum identifies that recoverability of downstream line-down loss is not automatic and remains subject to the governing terms and questions such as causation, remoteness or foreseeability, mitigation, exclusions and any applicable cap.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Claim-allocation discussion.","grader_hint":"Credit a concise treatment that flags the relevant dependencies without purporting to give a final enforceability opinion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document does not state that the £310,000 is admitted, audited, contractually recoverable or payable by Peatmoor Trust or the carrier.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All references to the customer claim.","grader_hint":"Review every monetary statement. Describing £310,000 as claimed, alleged, submitted or pending validation satisfies the limitation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The £310,000 amount is consistently described as the customer’s line-down claim and no unsupported breakdown, alternate total or financial calculation is introduced.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary, financial discussion and conclusion.","grader_hint":"Check all monetary figures against the bundle and ensure that the memo does not fabricate component amounts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum does not purport to decide contract enforceability, legal liability or insurance coverage on behalf of Legal or an insurer.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope statements and conclusions.","grader_hint":"A procurement recommendation and identification of issues for Legal are acceptable; a definitive legal or coverage ruling is not."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Functional boundaries are operational rather than merely disclaimed: Quality owns technical defect confirmation, Legal owns enforceability or legal-position review, Finance owns quantum validation, and Logistics or claims personnel own carrier-record follow-up as applicable.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Ownership and action statements.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent role labels where responsibilities remain clear. Each named function must have a concrete issue to resolve."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Requests intended for Peatmoor Trust, the forwarder or an insurer are specific and verifiable, such as post-repack condition evidence, seal or packing records, logger diagnostics, custody records, or substantiation of the claimed loss.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Verification requests or action table.","grader_hint":"Credit if external checks identify the precise record or fact sought and why it bears on the open issue; generic requests for 'more information' do not satisfy this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum provides a workable exception path if a requested record or check cannot be completed, including recording the unavailable evidence, preserving the current limitation and escalating the resulting allocation decision to the appropriate owner.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Contingency or escalation language.","grader_hint":"The path must work even if evidence never arrives. It should not assume successful completion or allow the claim to remain indefinitely ownerless."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The proposed meeting disposition is concrete: retain a provisional Peatmoor repack/pre-handover origin finding, do not finally allocate or admit the £310,000 claim on the present record, and pursue only the identified validation checks.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation and final decision.","grader_hint":"Equivalent decision language is acceptable. The disposition must be executable and must not revert to confirmed carrier liability."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Actions required to move from provisional finding to final allocation have named functional owners and concrete timing tied to the allocation meeting or a stated business-day deadline.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Action assignments.","grader_hint":"Look for both ownership and timing. Vague phrases such as 'follow up later' do not satisfy the criterion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The revision note accurately records removal of the draft’s unsupported temperature/transit conclusion, incorporation of the revised logger information, separation of origin from liability and addition of evidence limitations or verification actions.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Revision note compared with the marked-up draft and final memorandum.","grader_hint":"The note may be compact, but each recorded change must actually be reflected in the final document."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Important factual propositions are traceable to usable bundle references, including relevant ASN identifiers, photo references, logger timing and the applicable purchasing-term reference.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Inline citations, footnotes, evidence table or equivalent traceability mechanism.","grader_hint":"Check a representative sample against the bundle. References must let a reviewer or insurer locate the source without guessing; a generic reference to the entire bundle is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum is concise, audience-appropriate and independently usable by Procurement, Quality, Logistics, Finance and Legal, and it ends on the decision to carry into the meeting rather than a generic next-steps list.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole document, especially the final paragraph or decision block.","grader_hint":"Judge usability, clarity and closure. The final substantive statement must communicate the meeting position."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"An authorized senior buyer is revising an internal failure-origin memorandum before a cross-functional allocation meeting concerning a single supplied component and a disputed customer claim. The work must separate procurement findings from technical, legal, insurance and financial determinations while still supporting a usable decision.","difficulty_sources":["Separating a likely physical-origin finding from contractual risk, legal liability, claim recoverability and insurance coverage.","Revising an overconfident draft after changed logger information without replacing one unsupported certainty with another.","Tracing several near-connected evidence fragments while making unsupported causal links explicit.","Providing an executable allocation position and a failure path within a four-page cross-functional memorandum."],"authoring_plan":{"reference_file":{"artifact_id":"claim_evidence_bundle","format":"PDF","construction":"Create one coherent consolidated PDF containing a marked-up draft memorandum, review comments, a customer claim notice, receiving photographs with captions and metadata, two ASNs, a forwarder temperature-log extract with diagnostic information, relevant purchasing-term extracts, a preliminary technical note and Peatmoor Trust’s written position. Use stable internal evidence labels so a solver can cite individual items.","professional_realism":"The records should look like materials gathered for a single manufacturing claim and should be complete, legible and mutually consistent. The difficulty must arise from interpretation and bounded professional judgment, not hidden text, unreadable scans or contradictory identifiers."},"solver_instance":{"jurisdiction":"England and Wales","as_of_date":"30 September 2025","claim_status":"The customer has claimed £310,000 for line-down cost, but the bundle contains no completed validation, admission or agreed breakdown establishing recoverability.","draft_position":"The marked-up draft states too strongly that a temperature excursion during carriage caused the failure and recommends allocating the claim to the forwarder.","required_corrected_position":"The most likely condition-compromise window is Peatmoor Trust’s documented repacking or associated pre-handover handling, at calibrated rather than definitive confidence. Transit remains possible but is not established. The present record does not support final admission or contractual allocation of the £310,000."},"evidence_relationships":["Both ASNs concern the same purchase order, part, serial and shipment, allowing them to be reliably linked.","The original ASN describes the component in an OEM-sealed carton. The revised ASN records that Peatmoor Trust repacked it after label damage and changes shipment particulars such as package description or gross weight.","The ASN change proves that repacking occurred before carrier handoff but does not prove that the repack damaged the component.","Receiving photographs are tied to the same shipment and serial. They show an exterior carton without obvious crushing, puncture or wetting, while an internal port protector is detached and the port is exposed or shows debris.","The receiving photographs weaken a simple external-impact transit account but cannot establish when the internal condition arose.","The forwarder log contains approximately nine consecutive hours with no samples. Recorded temperatures immediately before and after the gap are within the applicable storage range.","The logger record includes a low-power, restart or comparable diagnostic that makes sensor interruption plausible. It does not prove the cause of the missing data.","No source records an out-of-range temperature, carrier opening, drop, impact or other handling event during the gap.","Peatmoor Trust’s statement says the part left conforming but relies on incoming inspection or conformity material created before the documented repack. No post-repack test, seal record or condition photograph accompanies the assertion.","The preliminary technical note states that the observed failure is compatible with contamination or ingress but cannot determine when or where material entered and does not identify a responsible actor.","The evidence does not directly connect the logger gap to a temperature breach or failure, and it does not directly connect the repack to protector detachment or contamination. These non-connections must remain visible.","The purchasing terms identify England and Wales as governing law and include a named delivery term or risk-transfer point. The delivery provision must not be presented as proof of physical causation.","The purchasing terms contain limitations or exclusions relevant to downstream line-down losses, but the material does not authorize the buyer to make a final enforceability or insurance-coverage determination.","The customer claim notice describes £310,000 as line-down cost but does not contain sufficient substantiation to validate the amount or establish mitigation."],"review_comments_to_embed":["Replace the unsupported assertion of a recorded temperature excursion.","Address the revised ASN and its repacking notation.","Separate likely physical origin from contractual liability, delivery risk and insurance coverage.","Identify evidence references that a counterparty or insurer can locate.","State which apparent links are not supported by the record.","Keep technical, legal and financial conclusions within the buyer’s authority.","Provide a route for unresolved checks or unavailable records rather than assuming all follow-up will succeed.","End with the position for the allocation meeting."],"doctrinal_boundaries":[{"rule_to_apply":"A contractual risk-transfer or delivery provision can affect commercial allocation but does not itself establish when a defect arose or prove factual causation.","must_not_claim":"Do not state that the delivery term alone proves Peatmoor Trust or the carrier caused the failure."},{"rule_to_apply":"A downstream line-down claim is not automatically recoverable merely because it has been presented; causation, contractual scope, remoteness or foreseeability, mitigation, exclusions and caps may require review.","must_not_claim":"Do not state that the entire £310,000 is admitted or payable."},{"rule_to_apply":"A party’s conformity assertion is evidence of its position, and its strength depends on whether supporting records cover the relevant post-repack condition.","must_not_claim":"Do not treat Peatmoor Trust’s uncorroborated statement as conclusive proof."},{"rule_to_apply":"Missing logger data establishes an evidentiary gap, not an excursion.","must_not_claim":"Do not invent temperatures or carrier conduct within the gap."},{"rule_to_apply":"Procurement may make an evidence-bounded commercial finding while preserving Quality’s technical authority, Legal’s enforceability role, Finance’s quantum-validation role and the insurer’s coverage role.","must_not_claim":"Do not issue a final technical diagnosis, legal opinion, claim admission or coverage decision."}],"expected_disposition":{"meeting_decision":"Carry forward a provisional finding that the most likely origin window is Peatmoor Trust’s repack or associated pre-handover handling; withdraw the draft’s assertion of proven transit temperature damage; do not finally allocate or admit the customer’s £310,000 claim on the current evidence.","follow_up_character":"Actions should seek post-repack condition or packing evidence, logger diagnostics and custody information, technical confirmation, contractual review and quantum substantiation. Each should have a functional owner and a near-term deadline.","failure_path":"If a record or check cannot be obtained, the final artifact should require that unavailability to be documented, the relevant limitation retained, and the residual allocation decision escalated to the proper functional owner rather than inferred away or left indefinitely open."},"gold_validation":"Construct a reference DOCX offline using Python and python-docx, render it with LibreOffice, and verify that it is no more than four pages. Walk every rubric item against the rendered document and the consolidated PDF, checking identifiers, chronology, numerical statements, doctrinal limitations, ownership, revision history and final-decision consistency."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"single_artifact","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"claim_evidence_bundle","filename":"claim_evidence_bundle.pdf","purpose":"Consolidated evidence bundle containing the marked-up draft, review comments, receiving photographs, both ASNs, forwarder temperature records, purchasing terms, technical note, claim notice and Peatmoor Trust statement.","required":true,"discovery":"Read the consolidated bundle and use its internal evidence references when preparing the revised memorandum."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"final_findings_memorandum","filename":"hydraulic_filter_claim_findings.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"Revised cross-functional findings memorandum supporting the claim-allocation decision.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file at the top level of the working directory using the exact filename hydraulic_filter_claim_findings.docx.","The complete document, including its revision note, must not exceed four rendered pages.","Use England and Wales as the jurisdiction and state the position as at 30 September 2025.","Provide one evidence-bounded finding on the most likely origin and a concrete disposition for the allocation meeting.","Do not invent figures, test results, temperatures, contractual language or chain-of-custody events.","End with the decision to be carried into the allocation meeting."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"communicate_stakeholders","work_product":"decision_memo","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"buyers_purchasing_agents","sector":"manufacturing","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":4.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"A domain-expert purchasing reviewer should verify evidence handling and commercial practicality, with a second reviewer checking the bounded England-and-Wales doctrinal statements and ensuring that the memorandum does not overstate technical, legal or insurance conclusions.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The memorandum can identify a most-likely condition-compromise window but cannot prove the precise damaging act from the supplied record.","The task supports an internal procurement position only; it does not permit a final technical-defect determination, legal opinion, insurance-coverage decision or validation of the customer’s claimed quantum."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:39:23+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:39:23+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:39:23+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:39:23+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R03']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:39:23+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/6e7a4d8561190362","declared_deliverables":["hydraulic_filter_claim_findings.docx"]};
